<h1>Same three-layer pattern, three real production platforms</h1>
<table class="fig">
<colgroup><col style="width:28%"><col style="width:24%"><col style="width:24%"><col style="width:24%"></colgroup>
<thead><tr><th>PLATFORM</th><th>LAYER A - KERNEL SANDBOX</th><th>LAYER B - LOCAL SEGMENTATION</th><th>LAYER C - PROXY</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Kubernetes Agent Sandbox (CNCF SIG, 2026 - official reference for AI agents / untrusted code on k8s)</td><td>gVisor via runtimeClassName: gvisor</td><td>Host-level L2/L3 segmentation below the pods</td><td>&quot;Sandbox Router&quot; - X-Sandbox-ID header-based routing</td></tr>
<tr><td>Gitpod / Ona (dev-workspace platform, millions of parallel workspaces)</td><td>gVisor (runsc), default for every workspace</td><td>Cilium (eBPF) network policies + dedicated tunnels - tenants can't ping each other</td><td>Envoy ingress, subdomain + session-cookie routing, zero raw ports to internet</td></tr>
<tr><td>Fly.io (production VM hosting - different sandbox tech, same 3-layer shape)</td><td>Firecracker microVMs (hardware-virtualized, own guest kernel per tenant)</td><td>Proprietary L2 network &quot;6PN&quot; - no local route between VMs</td><td>fly-proxy (Rust) - TLS termination + identity-based routing straight into the VM</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
